SwiftPutty local patch 0001
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); suitable for upstreaming

arm_arch_queries.h: return SYSCTL_MISSING when sysctlbyname() fails.

On macOS builds with HAVE_SYSCTLBYNAME, test_sysctl_flag() fell off the
end of a non-void function when sysctlbyname() failed (e.g. the queried
hw.optional.* flag does not exist on the running OS version). The
caller then read an indeterminate SysctlResult, which could report a
CPU feature as present. Clang reports this as -Wreturn-type.

--- a/unix/utils/arm_arch_queries.h
+++ b/unix/utils/arm_arch_queries.h
@@ -60,9 +60,8 @@
         size == sizeof(value)) {
         return value != 0 ? SYSCTL_ON : SYSCTL_OFF;
     }
-#else /* HAVE_SYSCTLBYNAME */
-    return SYSCTL_MISSING;
 #endif /* HAVE_SYSCTLBYNAME */
+    return SYSCTL_MISSING;
 }
 #endif /* defined __APPLE__ */
 
